		<title>Aon promotes Chris Rafferty to Chief Integration Officer for IMO</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/aon-promotes-chris-rafferty-to-chief-integration-officer-for-imo/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Saumya Jain]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:00:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Aon news]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209285</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Aon, the professional services firm specialising in risk, retirement and health solutions, has appointed Chris Rafferty as the new Chief Integration Officer for its Integration Management Office (IMO). Rafferty joined the group in 2007 as Chief Operating Officer, a role he held for nearly 15 years. He then became Global Specialty Product Leader at the [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/aon-promotes-chris-rafferty-to-chief-integration-officer-for-imo/">Aon promotes Chris Rafferty to Chief Integration Officer for IMO</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Aon, the professional services firm specialising in risk, retirement and health solutions, has appointed Chris Rafferty as the new Chief Integration Officer for its Integration Management Office (IMO).</p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-88903" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo.png" alt="aon logo" width="340" height="208" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo.png 884w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo-300x184.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo-768x471.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo-200x123.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/aon-logo-100x61.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 340px) 100vw, 340px" />Rafferty joined the group in 2007 as Chief Operating Officer, a role he held for nearly 15 years.</p>
<p>He then became Global Specialty Product Leader at the broking group, serving in the role for two years, and was most recently the Chicago Market Leader.</p>
<p>In the past, Rafferty has served as Associate for Mergers &amp; Acquisitions (M&amp;A) for Lincoln International, handling middle-market M&amp;A. He started his career as an Analyst at Wachovia Securities in 2001 and as a Summer Associate at Goldman Sachs.</p>
<p>Simultaneously, Aon has appointed Steven Carleton to succeed Rafferty as the Chicago Market Leader. Carleton joined Aon in 2010 as a Business Intern in Health and Benefits Consulting and Operations, and then served in the department in roles including Senior Consultant, Consultant, and Analyst.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-1502709059" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.willisre.com" aria-label="Willis Re"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/willis-re-728x90-sep2026.gif" alt="Willis Re"  width="728" height="90"   /></a></div></div>
<p>He has since spent his entire 15-year career with the firm, most recently as the Managing Director (MD) and Regional Sales Leader for Midwest.</p>
<p>Carleton has held roles of increasing responsibilities, including MD and Regional Sales Leader for Greater Chicago, Resident Sales Director for San Francisco, Senior Vice President and Resident Sales Director, Vice President of Northern California Health and Benefits Sales Leader, Assistant Vice President and Sales Leader for Middle Market Exchange (Midwest &amp; West).</p>
<p>Rafferty commented, &#8220;I am excited to share an update on my role at Aon and the future of our Chicago team. After several rewarding years as Aon&#8217;s Chicago Market Leader, I have begun transitioning into a new role as Chief Integration Officer for Aon&#8217;s Integration Management Office (IMO). I am energized by the work ahead and the opportunity to help ensure a thoughtful integration that supports our clients and colleagues.</p>
<p>&#8220;Additionally, I am very pleased to share that my colleague and friend, Steven Carleton, our Midwest Regional Sales Leader, will be succeeding me as Chicago Market Leader. Having worked closely with Steve for many years, I have seen his commitment to clients, his support for colleagues, and his deep knowledge of our business. For all of these reasons, I am confident he will continue to elevate our impact in the Chicago Market.&#8221;</p>
<p>He continued, &#8220;As I reflect on this transition, I am incredibly grateful for the opportunity to lead in Chicago &#8211; helping drive growth, supporting colleague development, and partnering on many of Aon&#8217;s most significant client relationships. The relationships we have built together mean a great deal to me.</p>
<p>&#8220;I especially want to say &#8220;thank you&#8221; to Lynn Jekkals, Kristin Kahn, Nancy Coletto, Kirin Sporar, Ron Kalvoda, Sandy McCoy, Scott Fullerton, Tracy Williams, and Peter Holz as key leaders that have supported and will continue to drive the team&#8217;s success. It has been a privilege to work alongside you and your teams! Thank you to our Chicago team, our clients, and my colleagues across Aon for your partnership and support. I am excited for what we will accomplish together in this next phase.&#8221;</p>
<p>Lynn Jekkals, Midwest Region Leader, Aon said, &#8220;I&#8217;m excited to share that Steven Carleton has been named the Chicago Market Leader. Steve brings deep experience across Aon, a passion for developing talent, and a track record of bringing teams together to create growth and deliver the best of Aon for our clients.</p>
<p>&#8220;Just as importantly, he knows Chicago, understands what makes this market special, and cares deeply about our colleagues and our culture. I&#8217;m excited for what&#8217;s ahead under Steve&#8217;s leadership and for the next chapter of growth and impact for our Chicago team.&#8221;</p>
<p>She continued, &#8220;I also want to recognize Chris Rafferty and thank him for his leadership of Chicago over the past several years and wish him success as the Chief Integration Officer. Chris has helped build a strong foundation for the future, and I&#8217;m incredibly grateful for his leadership and partnership. Congratulations, Steve! I can&#8217;t wait to see what&#8217;s ahead for Chicago.&#8221;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/aon-promotes-chris-rafferty-to-chief-integration-officer-for-imo/">Aon promotes Chris Rafferty to Chief Integration Officer for IMO</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209285</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>CCRIF to make $17.4m payment to Panama after M7.7 quake triggers parametric coverage</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/ccrif-to-make-17-4m-payment-to-panama-after-m7-7-quake-triggers-parametric-coverage/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Kassandra Jimenez-Sanchez]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:59:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[CCRIF]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[earthquake]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Panama]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Parametric insurance news]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209291</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>CCRIF SPC, the regional parametric risk pool for the Caribbean and Central America, has announced it is to make a payout of US$17.4 million to the Government of Panama following the magnitude 7.7 earthquake that struck the country on October 9, 2026. In line with CCRIF’s operational mandate to provide rapid liquidity to its members, the [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/ccrif-to-make-17-4m-payment-to-panama-after-m7-7-quake-triggers-parametric-coverage/">CCRIF to make $17.4m payment to Panama after M7.7 quake triggers parametric coverage</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>CCRIF SPC, the regional parametric risk pool for the Caribbean and Central America, has announced it is to make a payout of US$17.4 million to the Government of Panama following the magnitude 7.7 earthquake that struck the country on October 9, 2026.</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-170176" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new.jpg" alt="" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new.jpg 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/ccrif-logo-new-100x63.jpg 100w" sizes="(max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />In line with CCRIF’s operational mandate to provide rapid liquidity to its members, the payout will be made within 14 days of the event.</p>
<p>The earthquake occurred at 12:56 p.m. local time (17:56 UTC), with its epicentre near Pitaloza Arriba on the Azuero Peninsula, damaging<span style="font-weight: 400;"> homes, schools, hospitals, public buildings, and roads in various provinces across the country.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The preliminary assessment reports 656 affected schools. Also, 14 shelters were opened that housed 598 people. </span></p>
<p>Using its SPHERA earthquake model, CCRIF estimated peak ground acceleration of up to 0.5 g in Panama, the only CCRIF member country to experience shaking above the model’s 0.03 g reporting threshold.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-1502709059" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.willisre.com" aria-label="Willis Re"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/willis-re-728x90-sep2026.gif" alt="Willis Re"  width="728" height="90"   /></a></div></div>
<p>Based on the SPHERA model&#8217;s loss calculations, estimated national government losses exceeded the pre-arranged attachment point of Panama’s parametric earthquake policy, triggering the payout.</p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">CCRIF Chief Executive Officer, Mr. Isaac Anthony, said: &#8220;Our thoughts are with the people of Panama, and especially with the families and communities affected by this earthquake. This payout will give the Government immediate liquidity to support its response at the time it is most needed. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8220;Panama’s decision to secure its CCRIF earthquake coverage through the Fondo de Ahorro de Panamá is a strong example of how parametric insurance can work alongside national savings and stabilization mechanisms as part of a layered approach to financing disaster risk.&#8221;</span></p>
<p>Since joining CCRIF in 2018, Panama has received three payouts totalling  US$29 million for Hurricane Eta (2020) and 2024 rain events.</p>
<p>The October 9 earthquake payout raises Panama&#8217;s total to <span style="font-weight: 400;">approximately US$47 million, and marks CCRIF&#8217;s 83rd member payout since 2007, surpassing US$500 million &#8211; each delivered within 14 days of the event.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">CCRIF&#8217;s </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">parametric insurance policies pay out based on the occurrence of a pre-defined hazard event and the losses due to that event calculated by CCRIF’s models, rather than relaying on loss assessments on the ground. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">By streamlining this process, member governments, organisations and public utilities receive quick liquidity during the critical period immediately after a disaster</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/ccrif-to-make-17-4m-payment-to-panama-after-m7-7-quake-triggers-parametric-coverage/">CCRIF to make $17.4m payment to Panama after M7.7 quake triggers parametric coverage</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209291</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>ICW Group names Travis Noland to newly created reinsurance and risk management role</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/icw-group-names-travis-noland-to-newly-created-reinsurance-and-risk-management-role/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Taylor Mixides]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:00:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ICW Group]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209277</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>ICW Group Insurance Companies, a US insurance provider, has appointed Travis Noland as Head of Ceded Reinsurance and Enterprise Risk Management. The company said the creation of the position reflects its ongoing business development and focus on maintaining robust underwriting practices, managing risk and supporting long-term financial stability. Noland has been with ICW Group since [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/icw-group-names-travis-noland-to-newly-created-reinsurance-and-risk-management-role/">ICW Group names Travis Noland to newly created reinsurance and risk management role</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>ICW Group Insurance Companies, a US insurance provider, has appointed Travis Noland as Head of Ceded Reinsurance and Enterprise Risk Management.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-127369" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/ICW-Group-logo.png" alt="" width="360" height="240" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/ICW-Group-logo.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/ICW-Group-logo-200x133.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/ICW-Group-logo-100x67.png 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />The company said the creation of the position reflects its ongoing business development and focus on maintaining robust underwriting practices, managing risk and supporting long-term financial stability.</p>
<p>Noland has been with ICW Group since 2004, holding positions across reinsurance, catastrophe management and property underwriting. Before his latest appointment, he served as Vice President of Catastrophe Underwriting, with responsibility for difference in conditions (DIC) and monoline flood business.</p>
<p>Mark Moitoso, President of ICW Group, commented: &#8220;As ICW Group continues to diversify and grow, it is increasingly important that we evolve how we manage risk and capital across the enterprise. Travis has played an instrumental role in building and leading some of our most sophisticated underwriting and reinsurance capabilities. His deep expertise, strategic perspective, and collaborative leadership style make him uniquely qualified to lead our ceded reinsurance and enterprise risk management functions as we position ICW Group for the future.&#8221;</p>
<p>ICW Group also pointed to Noland&#8217;s contribution to the development of its underwriting operations and teams. During his tenure, he has been involved in initiatives to improve performance and develop underwriting expertise. The company said its earthquake underwriting operation received recognition from reinsurance and broking professionals for its analytical capabilities and underwriting standards under his leadership.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>Noland added: &#8220;I am honoured to take on this new opportunity and continue serving an organisation that has been my professional home for more than 20 years. ICW Group has built a strong foundation rooted in underwriting discipline, innovation, and financial strength. I look forward to working closely with teams across the organization to support the evolution of our business and long-term growth.&#8221;</p>
<p>Noland graduated from the University of California, San Diego, with a Bachelor of Arts degree. He also holds the Chartered Property Casualty Underwriter (CPCU) designation, a professional qualification in property and casualty insurance.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/icw-group-names-travis-noland-to-newly-created-reinsurance-and-risk-management-role/">ICW Group names Travis Noland to newly created reinsurance and risk management role</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209277</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Subscribe MGA secures long-term capacity agreement with Fortegra Insurance UK</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/subscribe-mga-secures-long-term-capacity-agreement-with-fortegra-insurance-uk/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Beth Musselwhite]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:00:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[capacity]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Fortegra]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Subscribe MGA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209234</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Subscribe MGA, a Lloyd’s-backed underwriting agency, has strengthened its underwriting platform by securing a new long-term capacity agreement with Fortegra Insurance UK Ltd. (FIUK), a subsidiary of global specialty insurer Fortegra. Launched in November 2025 by Acies MGU, Subscribe is a Lloyd’s-backed MGA specialising in financial lines insurance, including Professional Indemnity, Management Liability and Directors [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/subscribe-mga-secures-long-term-capacity-agreement-with-fortegra-insurance-uk/">Subscribe MGA secures long-term capacity agreement with Fortegra Insurance UK</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Subscribe MGA, a Lloyd’s-backed underwriting agency, has strengthened its underwriting platform by securing a new long-term capacity agreement with Fortegra Insurance UK Ltd. (FIUK), a subsidiary of global specialty insurer Fortegra.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-184346" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new.jpg" alt="Fortegra logo" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new.jpg 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/fortegra-logo-new-100x63.jpg 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" /><a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/acies-mgu-launches-lloyds-backed-underwriting-agency-subscribe-mga/">Launched in November 2025 by Acies MGU</a>, Subscribe is a Lloyd’s-backed MGA specialising in financial lines insurance, including Professional Indemnity, Management Liability and Directors and Officers (D&amp;O) coverage.</p>
<p>The £5 million binder provides Subscribe with A-rated underwriting capacity across its growing portfolio of UK micro and SME Professional Indemnity business.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to support several new underwriting initiatives planned for 2026 and 2027, including specialist medical malpractice and healthcare-related products, while providing flexibility to develop additional niche insurance propositions over time.</p>
<p>The agreement contributes to Subscribe’s wider growth strategy, centred on combining specialist underwriting expertise with long-term insurer partnerships to support sustainable expansion.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-1502709059" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.willisre.com" aria-label="Willis Re"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/willis-re-728x90-sep2026.gif" alt="Willis Re"  width="728" height="90"   /></a></div></div>
<p>David Eynon, Managing Director of Subscribe, said, &#8220;Long-term capacity partnerships are fundamental to the success of any specialist MGA. This new agreement with Fortegra provides A rated capacity and stability for our brokers, confidence for our clients and gives us the flexibility to continue investing in new specialist products.&#8221;</p>
<p>&#8220;We&#8217;re not looking to build a business around short-term opportunities. Our focus is on developing sustainable underwriting propositions that solve genuine market problems, backed by capacity providers who share that long-term perspective.&#8221;</p>
<p>The new agreement comes as Subscribe prepares to launch several specialist facilities over the coming months, broadening its proposition beyond traditional financial lines into adjacent specialist markets where it believes brokers require greater underwriting expertise and flexibility.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/subscribe-mga-secures-long-term-capacity-agreement-with-fortegra-insurance-uk/">Subscribe MGA secures long-term capacity agreement with Fortegra Insurance UK</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209234</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Miller launches Italian Delegated Authorities team led by Dario Rebeschini</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/miller-launches-italian-delegated-authorities-team-led-by-dario-rebeschini/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Beth Musselwhite]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:00:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Delegated Authority]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Miller]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209227</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Miller, an independent specialist re/insurance broker, has expanded its Delegated Authorities offering with the launch of a new team dedicated to the Italian market. Dario Rebeschini will lead the newly launched team as an Associate Director. He will be joined by Nick Kennedy and Arianna Schiavato, who have both been appointed Brokers, and Adam Cater, [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/miller-launches-italian-delegated-authorities-team-led-by-dario-rebeschini/">Miller launches Italian Delegated Authorities team led by Dario Rebeschini</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Miller, an independent specialist re/insurance broker, has expanded its Delegated Authorities offering with the launch of a new team dedicated to the Italian market.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-169929" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new.png" alt="Miller logo" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new.png 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new-300x188.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new-768x480.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new-200x125.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/miller-logo-new-100x63.png 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />Dario Rebeschini will lead the newly launched team as an Associate Director. He will be joined by Nick Kennedy and Arianna Schiavato, who have both been appointed Brokers, and Adam Cater, who joins as an Account Handler. All four join from Besso, part of the Ardonagh Group.</p>
<p>The team will work closely with Laurie Gaitskell, Head of European Delegated Authorities.</p>
<p>Miller said the appointments underscore its ongoing investment in expanding its product offering and jurisdictional capabilities in the Delegated Authority space.</p>
<p>The new team will specialise in open market and coverholder business, focusing particularly on SMEs and delivering multi-line solutions across short-tail and long-tail business in Italy, further strengthening Miller’s offering in Southern Europe.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>Gaitskell commented, “I am delighted to welcome Dario, Nick, Arianna and Adam to Miller. Their expertise and relationships in the Italian market further strengthen our European presence, and greatly complements our existing delegated authority business. As we continue to go from strength to strength, I’m excited to see our capabilities further evolve in this space.”</p>
<p>Rebeschini added, “Miller’s strong reputation, both internationally and in the London market, make it an incredibly exciting place to be. Combined with the firm’s independence and forward-looking culture, we are well positioned to deliver genuinely tailored solutions to clients.”</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/miller-launches-italian-delegated-authorities-team-led-by-dario-rebeschini/">Miller launches Italian Delegated Authorities team led by Dario Rebeschini</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209227</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Arch Insurance UK appoints Karen Donald as Glasgow Branch Manager</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/arch-insurance-uk-appoints-karen-donald-as-glasgow-branch-manager/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Beth Musselwhite]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Arch]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Arch Insurance UK]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209187</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Arch Insurance’s UK Regional Division has announced the appointment of Karen Donald as Branch Manager of its Glasgow operations. In her new role, Donald will oversee the branch’s day-to-day operations, manage broker distribution and drive the delivery of Arch’s growth strategy across Scotland. She will report to Janine Starkie, Regional Manager, North &#38; Scotland. She [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/arch-insurance-uk-appoints-karen-donald-as-glasgow-branch-manager/">Arch Insurance UK appoints Karen Donald as Glasgow Branch Manager</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Arch Insurance’s UK Regional Division has announced the appointment of Karen Donald as Branch Manager of its Glasgow operations.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-33123" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Arch-Insurance.jpg" alt="Arch Insurance" width="360" height="188" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Arch-Insurance.jpg 1200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Arch-Insurance-300x157.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Arch-Insurance-768x401.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Arch-Insurance-1024x535.jpg 1024w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />In her new role, Donald will oversee the branch’s day-to-day operations, manage broker distribution and drive the delivery of Arch’s growth strategy across Scotland. She will report to Janine Starkie, Regional Manager, North &amp; Scotland.</p>
<p>She brings more than 35 years of insurance industry experience and has spent most of her career operating exclusively within the Scottish market.</p>
<p>Donald joins Arch Insurance from AXA, where she most recently served as Regional Underwriting Manager.</p>
<p>Starkie commented, “Karen’s appointment reflects our commitment to strengthening our presence and relationships across Scotland. With extensive experience, local market knowledge and a clear focus on delivering for customers, she is ideally placed to help us drive growth and further elevate our broker partnerships.”</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/arch-insurance-uk-appoints-karen-donald-as-glasgow-branch-manager/">Arch Insurance UK appoints Karen Donald as Glasgow Branch Manager</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209187</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>James Winn appointed CUO and Head of Office, Brit Re &#8211; Bermuda</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/james-winn-appointed-cuo-and-head-of-office-brit-re-bermuda/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Kane Wells]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:00:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Brit]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Brit Re]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209275</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Brit Group Holdings Limited has appointed James Winn as Chief Underwriting Officer and Head of Office at Brit Re &#8211; Bermuda. Winn, currently Managing Director of Property Treaty at Brit in London, is expected to relocate to Bermuda towards the end of 2026, subject to the relevant approvals. He has more than 35 years’ experience [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/james-winn-appointed-cuo-and-head-of-office-brit-re-bermuda/">James Winn appointed CUO and Head of Office, Brit Re &#8211; Bermuda</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Brit Group Holdings Limited has appointed James Winn as Chief Underwriting Officer and Head of Office at Brit Re &#8211; Bermuda.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-209276" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit.jpg" alt="" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit.jpg 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/james-winn-brit-100x63.jpg 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />Winn, currently Managing Director of Property Treaty at Brit in London, is expected to relocate to Bermuda towards the end of 2026, subject to the relevant approvals.</p>
<p>He has more than 35 years’ experience in North American property treaty across the Lloyd’s and Bermuda markets.</p>
<p>Jonathan Stephenson, the current Head of Office, will hand over to Winn towards the end of the year as part of a planned transition.</p>
<p>Brit credited Stephenson with building the business to more than $250 million in third-party premium and establishing a robust underwriting platform to support an expanding product suite, most recently with the launch of US direct and facultative (D&amp;F).</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>Alongside Winn’s appointment, Sam Lewis and Jolie Broomhead, both assistant vice presidents, will relocate from their respective London teams to support Brit Re’s growth in casualty treaty and D&amp;F, respectively.</p>
<p>Jon Sullivan, Group Chief Underwriting Officer at Brit, commented, “We’re delighted that James has agreed to take on the leadership of our Bermuda platform as we look to the next phase of its growth.</p>
<p>&#8220;Since its launch two years ago, Brit Re has grown significantly and we continue to be excited by the opportunity to further build the Brit brand in Bermuda.</p>
<p>&#8220;I would also like to thank Jonathan, who has played a pivotal role in establishing the platform we have today and we are pleased that he will be with us until early 2027 to ensure a seamless handover.”</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/james-winn-appointed-cuo-and-head-of-office-brit-re-bermuda/">James Winn appointed CUO and Head of Office, Brit Re &#8211; Bermuda</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209275</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Marsh leans into AI growth but warns of systemic cyber exposure: CEO Doyle</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/marsh-leans-into-ai-growth-but-warns-of-systemic-cyber-exposure-ceo-doyle/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Kassandra Jimenez-Sanchez]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:30:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial intelligence in insurance and reinsurance news]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Marsh news]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209264</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>The rapid adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) carries systemic threats that require coordinated industry oversight as its implementation moves to an immediate operational driver across the re/insurance market, Marsh’s President and CEO John Doyle has commented. Speaking on the broker’s strategic positioning, Doyle emphasised that AI is already reshaping risk advisory, client engagement, and internal [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/marsh-leans-into-ai-growth-but-warns-of-systemic-cyber-exposure-ceo-doyle/">Marsh leans into AI growth but warns of systemic cyber exposure: CEO Doyle</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The rapid adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) carries systemic threats that require coordinated industry oversight as its implementation moves to an immediate operational driver across the re/insurance market, Marsh’s President and CEO John Doyle has commented.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-185418" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest.jpg" alt="" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest.jpg 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/marsh-logo-newest-100x63.jpg 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />Speaking on the broker’s strategic positioning, Doyle emphasised that AI is already reshaping risk advisory, client engagement, and internal workflows.</p>
<p>However, he warned that unchecked deployment could introduce severe, correlated risks to global markets, specifically via amplified cyber exposure.</p>
<p>While optimistic about the broader macroeconomic benefit of AI, Doyle stressed that deployment must be paired with strict governance to avert irreversible damage.</p>
<p>“When it comes to AI, we believe it will be good for our country and the global economy. However, we need to deploy the technology responsibly to avoid potentially severe, systemic, or irreversible risks. We&#8217;re particularly concerned about the potential for heightened cyber exposure from AI, and we are working with governments, insurance companies, and businesses to create awareness and resilience to this risk,” he stated.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>The executive affirmed that Marsh plans to take an assertive stance in guiding clients through both sides of the ledger: mitigating AI-related liabilities while capitalising on the technological upside.</p>
<p>He said: “Responsible AI implementation begins with the developers, but businesses and governments have a role to play in ensuring safeguards are in place. Marsh will be active in helping clients manage the risks and capture the opportunities from AI.</p>
<p>&#8220;Turning to AI in our business, we&#8217;re not thinking about it as something that will be a factor in our business. It already is a factor in our business. It&#8217;s enhancing our client relationships, how we manage operations, and how colleagues work every day.&#8221;</p>
<p>Marsh is focusing on several areas where AI is driving growth, including building AI-enabled products, consulting on AI transformation, serving the digital infrastructure ecosystem, and adding to capabilities and productivity for its producers and consultants.</p>
<p>“We&#8217;ve already deployed several AI-enabled products for clients that deliver valuable insights. These solutions tap into our large and expanding proprietary data sets in risk, health, and talent,” Doyle concluded.</p>
<p>The CEO comments follow the release of<a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/marsh-grows-q326-revenue-8-as-reinsurance-generates-374m/"> Marsh&#8217;s financial results for the third quarter of 2026.</a> The company&#8217;s revenue was $6.9 billion, an increase of 8% year on year and 5% on an underlying basis.</p>
<p>Its reinsurance arm, Marsh Re, recorded a 6% revenue decline in the quarter, to $374 million, down from $398 million a year earlier, on both a GAAP and underlying basis.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/marsh-leans-into-ai-growth-but-warns-of-systemic-cyber-exposure-ceo-doyle/">Marsh leans into AI growth but warns of systemic cyber exposure: CEO Doyle</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">209264</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>ACIC&#8217;s ACES Specialty Insurance Company gets approval to underwrite E&#038;S insurance</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/acics-aces-specialty-insurance-company-gets-approval-to-underwrite-es-insurance/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Saumya Jain]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:00:41 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ACES Specialty Insurance Company]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ACIC]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[American Coastal]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[excess & surplus lines]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=208827</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>ACES Specialty Insurance Company (ACES), a newly formed subsidiary of American Coastal Insurance Corporation (ACIC), the insurance holding company of American Coastal Insurance Company, has received a Certificate of Authority from the Arizona Department of Insurance and Financial Institutions to conduct transactions in excess and surplus (E&#38;S) lines. ACIC initially plans to underwrite catastrophe-exposed commercial [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/acics-aces-specialty-insurance-company-gets-approval-to-underwrite-es-insurance/">ACIC&#8217;s ACES Specialty Insurance Company gets approval to underwrite E&amp;S insurance</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>ACES Specialty Insurance Company (ACES), a newly formed subsidiary of American Coastal Insurance Corporation (ACIC), the insurance holding company of American Coastal Insurance Company, has received a Certificate of Authority from the Arizona Department of Insurance and Financial Institutions to conduct transactions in excess and surplus (E&amp;S) lines.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-204802" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new.png" alt="" width="360" height="225" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new.png 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new-300x188.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new-768x480.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new-200x125.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/american-coastal-logo-new-100x63.png 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />ACIC initially plans to underwrite catastrophe-exposed commercial E&amp;S property business through ACES in Florida, Texas, and South Carolina, building on AmCoastal’s experience in coastal commercial property.</p>
<p>The new insurer expects to begin writing business on or about 1 December, 2026, subject to customary regulatory, rating agency, and other operational requirements.</p>
<p>Brad Martz, President and Chief Executive Officer, ACIC, commented, &#8220;Receiving ACES’s Certificate of Authority is an important milestone for American Coastal and marks the start of a bold new chapter for our organization’s long-term strategy. With ACES, we can now serve a much wider range of commercial property risks in markets we know well.</p>
<p>&#8220;We built this platform along with our in-house managing general agency, Skyway Underwriters, carefully and with purpose, and we’re excited to put it to work for our agents, policyholders, and shareholders.&#8221;</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-3768581247" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.guycarp.com/insights/renewal-hub.html" aria-label="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png" alt="Marsh Re - New name. Expanded vision"  srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1.png 1440w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-300x37.png 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-1024x127.png 1024w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-768x95.png 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-200x25.png 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/marsh-re-in-article-720x90-1-100x12.png 100w" sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 100vw, 1440px" width="720" height="89"   /></a></div></div>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/acics-aces-specialty-insurance-company-gets-approval-to-underwrite-es-insurance/">ACIC&#8217;s ACES Specialty Insurance Company gets approval to underwrite E&amp;S insurance</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">208827</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Antares Global names Meera Rajoo-Oakley as Chief Actuary of Commercial</title>
		<link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/antares-global-names-meera-rajoo-oakley-as-chief-actuary-of-commercial/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Saumya Jain]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:00:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Antares Global]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People moves]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.reinsurancene.ws/?p=209215</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Antares Global, an international specialty insurance and reinsurance group, has promoted Meera Rajoo-Oakley to the newly created role of Chief Actuary of Commercial. The move aims to bring pricing, reserving and exposure management for Antares&#8217; commercial division under a single leader. In her new role, Rajoo-Oakley will report directly to Mark Graham, Commercial Chief Executive [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/antares-global-names-meera-rajoo-oakley-as-chief-actuary-of-commercial/">Antares Global names Meera Rajoo-Oakley as Chief Actuary of Commercial</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Antares Global, an international specialty insurance and reinsurance group, has promoted Meera Rajoo-Oakley to the newly created role of Chief Actuary of Commercial.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright wp-image-173188" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic.jpg" alt="antares logo" width="340" height="213" srcset="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic.jpg 800w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/antares-logo-qic-100x63.jpg 100w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 340px) 100vw, 340px" />The move aims to bring pricing, reserving and exposure management for Antares&#8217; commercial division under a single leader.</p>
<p>In her new role, Rajoo-Oakley will report directly to Mark Graham, Commercial Chief Executive Officer for Antares.</p>
<p>Her remit includes bringing strategic oversight of the actuarial and exposure management functions across the business, which comprises Lloyd’s Syndicate 1274 and Antares Re.</p>
<p>Rajoo-Oakley has over 18 years of actuarial experience across the UK and international reinsurance and insurance market. She joined Antares Global in 2017 and has served as Chief Actuary of its Lloyd’s syndicate since 2020.</p><div class="reins-in-every-article reins-entity-placement" id="reins-1152140515"><div id="reins-1502709059" style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><a href="https://www.willisre.com" aria-label="Willis Re"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/willis-re-728x90-sep2026.gif" alt="Willis Re"  width="728" height="90"   /></a></div></div>
<p>Prior to this, she held roles at Gable Insurance, Direct Line Group and Grant Thornton, and currently is also Chair of the Committee of Actuaries in the Lloyd’s Market.</p>
<p>Graham commented on the appointment, &#8220;Bringing reserving, pricing and exposure management together under Meera’s leadership will enable us to streamline our operations, strengthen the specialist support available to our underwriting and claims teams, and drive the continued development of our Commercial platform.</p>
<p>&#8220;Meera has made a significant contribution to our syndicate’s success during her almost 10 years with the business; and her appointment reinforces our commitment to developing talent and providing clear pathways for professional progression.</p>
<p>&#8220;Her deep actuarial expertise, strong leadership credentials and detailed understanding of our Commercial business also make her ideally placed to take on this role.&#8221;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws/antares-global-names-meera-rajoo-oakley-as-chief-actuary-of-commercial/">Antares Global names Meera Rajoo-Oakley as Chief Actuary of Commercial</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.reinsurancene.ws">ReinsuranceNe.ws</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
